{
  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA encoder has been the single largest performance lever (PCA→SCVI gave ~6 pts in RNA-only, ~4 pts in multimodal), and the current best config_031 (scvi, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.678. However, we have zero evidence about scgpt, the third available RNA encoder. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 as the RNA representation, or is scvi already near-optimal? This experiment (config_043) changes only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding the proven-best settings (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) constant, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_031. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) RNA encoder quality has historically produced the largest gains, so resolving whether scgpt could push performance above 0.678 is the highest-impact open question; (2) it reduces uncertainty on a completely unexplored dimension with no prior data; (3) if scgpt underperforms, it confirms scvi as optimal and redirects budget toward image-encoder upgrades (ViT-L); if it outperforms, it opens a new promising direction. This is more informative than testing a better image encoder (ViT-L) because the image contribution is already known to be modest (~3 pts), whereas the RNA encoder lever has shown much larger effects."
}

